# Prototype Development Rules

## Scope
These rules apply to all prototypes in the `prototypes/` directory and the `launcher/` app.

## Technology Stack
- **React 18** with TypeScript
- **PatternFly v6** (`@patternfly/react-core`, `@patternfly/react-icons`, `@patternfly/react-table`)
- **Vite 6** for dev server and builds
- **react-router-dom v7** for routing within prototypes

## PatternFly v6 Rules
- Always use `pf-v6-` prefixed utility classes. Never use `pf-v5-`, `pf-v4-`, or `pf-u-` prefixes.
- Import components from `@patternfly/react-core`, icons from `@patternfly/react-icons/dist/esm/icons/`.
- Use `Title` for headings, `Content` for body text. Never use raw `<h1>`-`<h6>` or `<p>` elements.
- Use semantic design tokens (e.g. `--pf-t--global--text--color--regular`) for custom CSS. Never use hardcoded colors.
- Use PF spacing tokens for margins/padding. Never use hardcoded pixel values in inline styles.
- No Tailwind CSS. Use PatternFly utility classes and design tokens for all styling.

## Prototype Structure
Every prototype must follow this structure:
```
prototypes/{name}/
├── package.json
├── vite.config.ts      # base: '/AppDev-UX-Prototypes/{name}/'
├── tsconfig.json
├── index.html
└── src/
    ├── main.tsx
    ├── App.tsx           # Root component with Page layout
    └── pages/            # Page components
```

## Vite Base Path
- Every prototype's `vite.config.ts` must set `base: '/AppDev-UX-Prototypes/{prototype-name}/'`
- The launcher sets `base: '/AppDev-UX-Prototypes/'`

## Wizard Pattern
When building wizards:
- Use `Modal` (variant `large`) + `Wizard` + `WizardStep` from PatternFly
- Apply `overflow: hidden` on the Modal style to prevent horizontal scrollbar
- Set `width="100%"` and `className="migrate-wizard"` on the Wizard for full-width header
- Add this CSS class to prevent horizontal scroll:
  ```css
  .migrate-wizard { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: hidden; }
  ```
- Use `WizardHeader` with `title`, `description`, and `onClose` for the dark header
- For sub-steps, pass `steps={[...]}` array to a parent `WizardStep`
- Use bordered `<div>` containers for tables (not `<fieldset>/<legend>`)
- Put `Radio` components inline in table Name cells (no separate select column)
- Apply `tableLayout: 'fixed'` and `width: '100%'` on tables to prevent overflow

## Adding a New Prototype
1. Copy `prototypes/_template/` to `prototypes/{name}/`
2. Update `vite.config.ts` base to `/AppDev-UX-Prototypes/{name}/`
3. Add an entry to `launcher/src/prototypes.ts`
4. Add install + build steps to root `package.json` scripts
5. Add build + assemble steps to `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`

## Accessibility
- All interactive elements must have ARIA labels
- Tables must have `aria-label`
- Form inputs must have associated `FormGroup` labels
- Use `screenReaderText` on table header cells where visual label is hidden
